[preflight] snapshot 10 files from assets/ReCodeAgent/data/tool_projects/crust/leftpad/c
[delegate] analyst <- Explore the source codebase, identify all modules and their dependencies, and produce a source map and brief in meta/plan.md.
[phase] Contract
[delegate] architect <- Read analysis/source-map.md and the discovery brief, then produce the target-language (Rust) contract in analysis/brief.md: define the crate layout (leftpad library + CLI binary), the public API surface (leftpad function signature, error handling, CLI arg parsing), the C→Rust type/semantics mapping (char*/size_t/NULL/malloc/assert/strcmp/puts, pledge), and the build/test strategy.
[delegate] validator <- Validate the Rust migration contract in analysis/brief.md against analysis/source-map.md and the source files: confirm the crate layout (leftpad #![no_std] library + CLI binary), the public API (leftpad() -> String, leftpad_len() -> usize), the C→Rust type/semantics mapping (char*/size_t/NULL/malloc/assert/strcmp/puts, pledge via #[cfg(target_os)]), and the build/test strategy are complete, internally consistent, and cover every module in the source map. Report any gaps or contradictions.
[phase] Planning
[delegate] planner <- Read analysis/brief.md (the validated Rust migration contract) and analysis/source-map.md, then produce the migration batch plan: partition every target module (the leftpad #![no_std] library, the CLI binary, and the test suite) into an ordered set of batches such that each batch depends only on earlier batches and the batch order compiles, assign each target module to exactly one batch, and record the batch plan in meta/plan.md plus the corresponding tasks in meta/tasks.json.
[phase] Pilot
[delegate] translator <- Translate batch-1 (scaffold) of the leftpad C→Rust migration: create target/Cargo.toml declaring the `leftpad` crate with crate-type = ["rlib","cdylib"], a `#![no_std]` library target, a `[[bin]]` target for the CLI, and an optional/target-specific `libc` dependency gated for OpenBSD (per the brief's pledge mapping); and verbatim-copy the documentation artifacts source/leftpad.1 → target/man/leftpad.1, source/leftpad.3 → target/man/leftpad.3, source/README.md → target/README.md, source/LICENSE.md → target/LICENSE.md. Follow analysis/brief.md for the manifest decisions. Do not write lib.rs or main.rs yet.
[delegate] translator <- Translate batch-2 (library crate) of the leftpad C→Rust migration: create target/src/lib.rs as a #![no_std] library implementing the frozen public API from analysis/brief.md — leftpad() -> String and leftpad_len() -> usize — mapping the C source (source/src/leftpad.h + source/src/leftpad.c) per the brief's C→Rust semantics: char*/const char* -> Option<&str>, size_t -> usize, NULL sentinel -> Option, and the manual buffer + dest_sz out-parameter -> an owned String return. Preserve the #![no_std] freestanding property (no std/alloc unless the brief mandates it). Do not write main.rs or tests yet. Follow analysis/brief.md for all API and semantics decisions.
